hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1087","Ahmad bin Mani’ told us strange news. Ibn Abi Zaydah told us. Ubayd Allah told us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: “Begin the morning prayer with the Witr prayer.”"
"1088","Ahmad bin Mani’ and Ziyad bin Ayyub narrated to us, saying: Ibn Abi Zaida narrated to us, Asim Al-Ahwal narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Shaqiq, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Begin with the dawn prayer.” And Ahmad said: “Hasten”"
"1089","Abu Musa told us, Abd al-A’la told me, Muammar, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Abu Nadra, on the authority of Abu Sa’id al-Khudri, The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Do the Witr prayer before the morning.” Abu Musa told us, Abu Amir told us, Ali, meaning Ibn Al-Mubarak, on the authority of Yahya, said: Abu Nadhrah al-Awqi told me that Abu Sa`id al-Khudri told them that they asked the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings be upon him, neglected the Witr prayer, and he said: “Perform the Witr prayer before dawn.”"
